    "intro_html":  "Izmir kofte is the Turkish answer to the question every tired cook asks on a Sunday: what if the meatballs and the potatoes just cooked themselves in the same pan? Seasoned turkey kofte and thick potato slices bake together under a tomato and pepper sauce until the potatoes drink up everything around them. Each portion lands at \u003cstrong\u003e{{cal}} calories and {{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost), and it comes out of the oven looking like somebody worked a lot harder than you did.",
